THE CORE PROBLEM: WHY SINGLE AGENTS FAIL
================================================================================

Two years ago, a team built an "ultimate AI assistant" that could query
databases, manage calendars, and handle dozens of tasks.

On paper, it was spectacular.

In production, it was a disaster.

The agent got distracted, updated the wrong records, and sent half-finished
reports to executives.

The lesson:

A single agent cannot reliably juggle dozens of tools.

The cognitive load is simply too high for current models to handle with
100% reliability.

This module teaches you how to move from isolated tools to integrated agent
networks that deliver true reliability in production environments.


