4. EDGE CASE HANDLING AND AGENT DRIFT PREVENTION
================================================================================

THE CHALLENGE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Agents can behave unpredictably over time.

Common problems include:

1. Agent Drift
   Behavior gradually diverges from intended goals.

2. Edge Cases
   Unusual inputs break the agent's logic.

3. Hallucinations
   Confident but false outputs.


DETECTION AND PREVENTION STRATEGIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


1. IDENTIFY EDGE CASES BEFORE PRODUCTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Map scenarios that break agents
- Test with adversarial inputs
- Build detection mechanisms


2. IMPLEMENT BEHAVIORAL MONITORING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Track agent outputs over time
- Detect deviations from baseline behavior
- Alert when drift exceeds thresholds


3. MAKE SYSTEMS AUDITABLE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Use reasoning traces to explain decisions
- Log all agent actions and outputs
- Enable post-hoc analysis of failures


4. REFINE GOAL SPECIFICATIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Write precise, unambiguous goals
- Include explicit constraints
- Define success criteria clearly


